# Frontend Conventions

## Stack

- Next.js 14+ with App Router
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Recharts (or Plotly) for the distribution histogram

## Structure

- Pages live in `frontend/app/`
- Reusable components in `frontend/components/`
- API calls and helpers in `frontend/lib/`
- All API calls go to the FastAPI backend — never directly to Supabase

## React Patterns

- Functional components only, no class components
- `use client` directive only when interactivity requires it — prefer server components for data fetching
- Custom hooks in `frontend/lib/hooks/` for reusable stateful logic
- Props always typed with TypeScript interfaces

## API Integration

- All backend calls go through a typed client in `frontend/lib/api.ts`
- Use `async/await`, handle loading and error states explicitly in UI
- Never expose the Supabase URL or service key in frontend code

## UI Principles

- The user is new to React — keep component trees shallow and obvious
- One component = one clear responsibility
- Loading states and error messages must always be handled visibly
